      "body": "Hey User:712020:95338d1d-c86b-4b96-9d93-2435154f753f , thanks for putting this story together, lots of good detail. User:5cc71886cbbec211ec62929d  an I had a good call last week around some of the UI stories and I had said I would review a few and provide some thoughts on tweaks if needed. \n\nI’ve reviewed this one and a few of my thoughts are:\n\n  - For the **Context* area:\n      - We mentioned that ‘*any associated content (e.g. campaign imagery, featured links) as defined in the CMS*’.\n        - Do we have any designs of what might be put in there? Want to take a look and think about a few possible implementation options. \n        - Also, have we had a session with the business/marketing team around what & how they want to put items in here? These discussions would be very helpful for the bullet above, around implementation options. \n      - One of the bullet points also say ‘*Nav items and their associated mega menu content are managed via the CMS; adding or removing items does not require a code change*’, is this similar to the bullet point above?\n  - For the **Acceptance Criteria* area:\n      - Can we work with Claude around defining Accessibility requirements for:\n        - Keyboard Navigation\n        - Screen reader requirements\n      - Let’s also get one of the developers to review the current PWA Kit Navigation to see what of these functionalities it already has and document that for support of this ticket.\n\nEverything else looks good, thanks for putting this together.",
