      "id": "18650",
      "key": "SFCC-324",
      "summary": "Foundational Content Model: Site Reference Type & Base Site Entries",
      "description": "As a\n Content editor,\nI want\n a single, centrally-managed list of Zimmermann's storefronts in Contentful,\nso that\n when I scope a piece of content to one or more specific storefronts, I'm picking from a real list that updates in one place if a storefront is added or removed — not retyping site IDs by hand into every content type.\nResolves the \nregions\n content-model field open item tracked in \n02-contentful.md\n §10.1 and flagged as an unconfirmed risk in the SFCC-249 TSD (Section 7). Validated via a spike (2026-08-04, see \n.docs/planning/contentfulSiteScoping.md\n): a dedicated \nsite\n content type, one entry per SFCC site with its entry ID set explicitly equal to the SFCC site ID, correctly disambiguates site-specific content even where two storefronts share a locale (e.g. \nZimmermannUK\n / \nZimmermannEUen\n, both \nen-GB\n) — confirmed via both the Management API and the live Preview API. This story creates that content type for real (not the spike's throwaway version) and seeds the base site entries, so every future site-scoped content type (built under SFCC-304 or elsewhere) has something to reference from day one.\nScope: the \nsite\n content type + seeded base entries only. Adding the resulting reference field to individual page-level content types happens in those types' own stories (SFCC-304 and others), not here.",
