    },
    {
      "id": "18645",
      "key": "SFCC-319",
      "summary": "Contentful Environment Setup",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Contentful Environment Setup\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the platform-level provisioning, configuration, and CI/CD wiring required to run Contentful as the Zimmermann storefront's CMS — the Space/environment/locale/role bootstrap on the Contentful side, and the MRT/PWA Kit-side integration plumbing (webhook receiver, schema-sync pipeline) that consumes it. It is the prerequisite platform layer that SFCC-304 (Contentful Components) and every page-level Contentful story (SFCC-58, SFCC-111, SFCC-117, SFCC-190, SFCC-203, SFCC-204, SFCC-102, SFCC-267, etc.) depend on before their content types and components can be built and tested end-to-end.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nContent authors and the incoming dedicated Contentful squad cannot safely operate on this platform until environments, roles, webhooks, and the schema-sync pipeline are fully configured and automated — right now that work is partially done by hand, per-developer, with no CI enforcement. Closing this out removes a bottleneck blocking every Contentful-dependent story across both squads and de-risks the handoff to the incoming Contentful squad (Appendices A/B of the SFCC-249 TSD).\nScope\nIn Scope:\nCompleting per-tier Contentful/MRT environment configuration (env vars, roles/permissions)\nThe Contentful publish-webhook cache-purge receiver and its per-environment wiring\nAutomating the content-type schema-as-code pipeline (sync/migrate/drift-detection) into CI\nEvaluating Contentful's new Organisation-level Content Model Templates capability against the current script-based schema approach\nThe foundational site-scoping content model (the reference content type + base site entries other content types depend on) — content-model infrastructure, not per-page content types\nOut of Scope:\nPer-page/per-component Contentful content type definitions and their React components — covered in SFCC-304 (Contentful Components) and individual page-level stories\nContent authoring (copy, images) — Zimmermann/incoming Contentful squad responsibility\nMRT SSR-first fetch migration and the reference-resolution (product/category ID → hook) pattern — covered by SFCC-238\nMRT application topology (single vs per-integration apps) — covered by SFCC-237\nDependencies\nSFCC-123 / SFCC-249 (Contentful Integration TSD) — this epic operationalises Appendix B's \"Incomplete\" checklist items\nSFCC-238 (reference-resolution pattern) for anything touching product/category ID rendering\nRegional-config owner sign-off on US-International (ZimmermannUSIntl) site/locale before that site can be wired into Contentful environment config\nAssumptions & Constraints\nOne Contentful Space, one Environment per delivery tier (dev/test/sit/staging/uat/production via alias) — decided by Tim Lavelle, not revisited here\nEnvironments, locales, API keys, and the production alias are already bootstrapped (per SFCC-249 Appendix B) — this epic covers what's still incomplete, not a re-bootstrap\nContent Model Templates are now an organisation-level Contentful feature, not environment-level — schema-governance stories should account for this",
