{"result":"{
  "id": "18139",
  "key": "SFCC-94",
  "summary": "Homepage Content Row — Flexible Grid & Image Carousel",
  "description": "**As a** Site Merchandiser,\n\n**I want** to configure homepage image rows to display a variable number of columns (2, 3, or 4) and optionally cycle through more images than are visible at once,\n\n**so that** I can control the visual layout and cadence of campaign and editorial content on the homepage to suit each seasonal drop.\n\n----\n\n**Context:**\n\nSFCC-90 establishes the homepage module structure with content rows currently built as fixed 4-column grids. This story adds two layers of flexibility to those rows, both controlled entirely via Contentful — no code changes should be required for the merchandiser to change the layout of a row.\n\n**Grid flexibility:** The number of visible columns per row is configurable in Contentful (2, 3, or 4). The PWA renders the appropriate column layout based on the value set on the content entry. Each column displays a CMS-managed image with its own CTA link.\n\n**Carousel behaviour:** If more images are added to the content entry than the configured column count, the row becomes a carousel — the additional images cycle in as the shopper navigates or the carousel auto-advances. If the number of images equals the column count, the row renders as a static grid with no carousel controls.\n\nExample: a 3-column row with 9 images loaded in Contentful renders as a 3-column carousel cycling through 3 sets of 3 images.\n\nThis component can be built against mock Contentful content before the full content model is finalised, in line with the approach established in SFCC-90.",
  "status": {
    "name": "To Do",
    "category": "To Do",
    "color": "blue-gray"
  },
  "updated": "2026-07-06T14:13:07.778+1000"
}"}

