  "key": "SFCC-86",
  "summary": "Motion Design",
  "description": "**Epic Summary**\nThis epic defines and implements motion design guidelines and animation behaviour for the Zimmermann SFCC storefront. It covers hover and transition animations across interactive UI components, with motion guidelines documented in Figma by the Accenture design team as the handoff spec for developers. Developer implementation is against signed-off Figma specs only.\n\n**Business Value / Objective**\nMotion design is a key part of delivering a premium, brand-consistent digital experience that matches Zimmermann's elevated aesthetic. Well-executed animations — scroll behaviour, hover transitions, add-to-bag feedback — reinforce the brand's visual identity and create a more polished, engaging storefront for clients across all devices.\n\n**Scope**\n\n*In Scope*\n\n- Accenture design team authoring of motion guidelines and animation specs in Figma, covering hover and transition animations across interactive UI components\n- Implementation of motion and animation behaviour across the storefront against signed-off Figma specs — for example, logo scroll behaviour in the site header (SFCC-93) and fly-to-bag animation on add to bag from PLP (SFCC-98). Scope is limited to animations where a signed-off Figma spec exists and Zimmermann has approved; additional animations will be added as stories under this epic as designs are finalised\n- Reduced motion support — animations must respect the user's OS-level reduced motion accessibility preference\n\n*Out of Scope*\n\n- Video content and Vimeo embeds — covered in SFCC-5 Product Detail Page (PDP)\n- Page transition loading states — covered in SFCC-2 PWA Kit Components\n\n**Dependencies**\n\n- Zimmermann sign-off on motion specs before build can begin — logo scroll behaviour final approach pending CEO sign-off (SFCC-93)\n- SFCC-2 PWA Kit Components — base component library must be in place before motion behaviour can be layered on\n- SFCC-3 Homepage & Navigation — logo scroll behaviour (SFCC-93) depends on the header component being built\n- SFCC-6 Product Listing Page (PLP) — fly-to-bag animation (SFCC-98) depends on the PLP product tile component being built\n\n**Assumptions & Constraints**\n\n- No motion design will be implemented without a signed-off Figma spec from the design team and Zimmermann\n- The full list of components requiring motion treatment is not yet finalised; scope will grow as the design team delivers additional specs\n- Sprint is TBD pending design delivery timeline\n\n**Priority:** Medium\n\n**Target Release / Sprint:** TBC",
