  "description": "**Epic Summary**\n\nProvision and configure all SFCC Business Manager environments (dev, staging, prod) and establish the foundational platform settings required before any build work can begin. This epic unblocks all other epics across both squads.\n\n**Business Value / Objective**\n\nWithout environments stood up and correctly configured, no build or testing can happen. This is the critical path item for sprint 1 — getting SFCC and MRT environments live, with correct site IDs, permissions, and storefront config across all 8 storefronts, is the prerequisite for every other epic on the board.\n\n**Scope**\n\nIn Scope:\n\n- Provision SFCC Business Manager instances for dev, staging, and production\n- Configure site IDs, locales, currencies, and tax jurisdictions for all 8 storefronts\n- Set OCAPI/SCAPI permissions for PWA Kit API access\n- PWA Kit scaffold and MRT config, local dev environment setup\n- CI/CD pipeline including lint, unit tests, bundle size gate, Playwright P0 suite, and Lighthouse CI >90\n- Regional feature flags to support canary go-live strategy\n\nOut of Scope:\n\n- Storefront-level business configuration (languages, translations, tax rules) — covered in Regional Storefronts (SFCC-19)\n- Design system / UI library component setup — covered in PWA Kit Components (SFCC-2)\n- Any functional build work (cart, checkout, PDP, etc.)\n\n**Dependencies**\n\n- Zimmermann to provide access to SFCC licences, Business Manager, GitHub, and CI/CD tooling\n- MuleSoft API contracts confirmed before build commences\n- Salesforce MRT environment provisioning\n\n**Assumptions & Constraints**\n\n- 8 storefronts in scope: AU, US Domestic, US International, UK, EU Domestic, EU International, HK, ME",
