      "summary": "Contentful Environment Governance: Complete Per-Tier Config & Roles",
      "description": "As a\n Platform/Integration engineer,\nI want\n every Contentful deployment tier (dev/test/sit/staging/uat/production) fully configured with its MRT environment variables and Contentful roles locked down,\nso that\n no tier is left with incomplete credentials or open content-type editing permissions before the Contentful squad onboards.\nPer the SFCC-249 TSD (Appendix B), MRT environment variables are only set for 4 of 9 tiers today, and Contentful roles have not yet been configured to restrict content-type/schema editing in sit/staging/uat/master to the CI service account. This story completes both: sets the remaining per-tier env vars (CDA token, CPA token where applicable, webhook secret, environment ID), and configures Contentful roles so schema changes in non-dev environments can only be applied by the CI service account, not ad hoc via the Studio UI — preventing environment drift.\nScope: environment variables + Contentful role/permission configuration only. Does not cover the webhook receiver itself (separate story) or the schema-sync CI pipeline (separate story).",
