      "id": "18597",
      "key": "SFCC-304",
      "summary": "Contentful Components",
      "description": "Epic Name:\n Contentful Components\nEpic Summary\nThis epic covers the Contentful content type definitions, schema setup, and per-storefront content authoring support for all Contentful-managed components across the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. It ensures that static and semi-static content — such as informational copy, UI labels, placeholders, and page-level text — is manageable by Zimmermann's content and merchandising teams without requiring a code deployment.\nBusiness Value / Objective\nContentful is the CMS layer for the Zimmermann PWA Kit storefront. By defining reusable content types and ensuring content is authored per storefront and locale, Zimmermann's team gains the ability to update content independently across all 8 storefronts. This reduces operational dependency on development and supports ongoing content governance post-launch.\nScope\nIn Scope:\nContentful content type definitions and schema setup for all CMS-managed components across the storefront\nPlaceholders content model for hardcoded UI labels and strings (e.g. page headings, CTA labels) that the business may want to edit without a deployment\nStatic informational components reused across multiple pages (e.g. accordion panels for Assistance, Shipping and Returns, Secured Payments)\nPer-storefront body content authoring support — content varies by region (e.g. Shipping and Returns policy differs per storefront)\nGraceful fallback behaviour when Contentful content has not been authored or a fetch fails — confirmed global pattern: content does not render, page remains unaffected\nOut of Scope:\nContentful content authoring (copy, phone numbers, images etc) — Zimmermann responsibility\nContentful platform setup and provisioning — covered separately\nTransactional or SFCC-data-driven components (cart line items, order summary, pricing) — covered in respective feature epics\nPWA Kit component build — covered in respective feature epics (Cart, PDP, PLP etc); this epic covers the Contentful content type only\nDependencies\nContentful environment provisioning and access must be in place before content type creation can begin\nZimmermann must author content per storefront and locale before PWA Kit components can be tested end-to-end\nPWA Kit component stories in feature epics depend on Contentful content types existing first\nTim Lavelle (Solution Architect) — global Contentful fetch failure pattern and placeholders content model structure must be confirmed before stories are written\nAssumptions & Constraints\nContentful is the single CMS for all non-transactional content across the PWA storefront\nSection title labels (e.g. accordion headers) are managed via the placeholders content model; body content is authored per storefront\nReusable content type structures are built once and referenced across multiple page surfaces; body content is authored separately per surface as content will differ\nContent types are an Accenture deliverable; content authoring is a Zimmermann responsibility — to be confirmed with Tim Lavelle",
